\begin_layout Standard
Before the drift the space charge cancels the applied field at the tip almost completely, which suppresses new ionization. After only 
\begin_inset Formula $12.5\,\mu\text{s}$
\end_inset
 both the direct field and the rod image weaken at the tip, and the total field there recovers to 
\begin_inset Formula $42.7\,\text{kV/cm}$
\end_inset
. This reproduces the paper's statement that a small drift rapidly increases the field at the rod tip until a new corona streamer can incept, and it explains why the drift controls the length of the dark period.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Compared with Figure 4, the shape of the drifted 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{sp}$
\end_inset
 agrees, including the field behind the drifted cloud (
\begin_inset Formula $0.40$
\end_inset
 versus 
\begin_inset Formula $0.42$
\end_inset
 of the minimum). The absolute values are about 
\begin_inset Formula $10\%$
\end_inset
 smaller than the paper's, the same offset already found for 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{sp}$
\end_inset
 at the tip in Figure 3 (
